I don't know why, but `metadata.getType()` doesn't return `DIRECTORY` for runfiles artifacts.

``` diff
diff --git a/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/buildeventstream/BuildEvent.java b/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/buildeventstream/BuildEvent.java
index f13c8f01ec..911c538a68 100644
--- a/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/buildeventstream/BuildEvent.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/buildeventstream/BuildEvent.java
@@ -76,10 +76,11 @@ public interface BuildEvent extends ChainableEvent, ExtendedEventHandler.Postabl
           return switch (metadata.getType()) {
             case DIRECTORY -> LocalFileType.OUTPUT_DIRECTORY;
             case SYMLINK -> LocalFileType.OUTPUT_SYMLINK;
-            default -> LocalFileType.OUTPUT_FILE;
+            default -> (artifact.isRunfilesTree() ? LocalFileType.OUTPUT_DIRECTORY : LocalFileType.OUTPUT_FILE);
           };
         }
-        if (artifact.isDirectory()) {
+
+        if (artifact.isDirectory() || artifact.isRunfilesTree()) {
           return LocalFileType.OUTPUT_DIRECTORY;
         } else if (artifact.isSymlink()) {
           return LocalFileType.OUTPUT_SYMLINK;
```

The warning disappears with this quick fix.
